### ====================================================================
### AI-Assisted Language Journaling API - VS Code HTTP Client Test Suite
### ====================================================================
### How to run in Visual Studio Code:
###   1. Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
###      or open with VS Code's native HTTP client.
###   2. Start the FastAPI backend:
###      cd backend && source .venv/bin/activate && PYTHONPATH=.. uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
###   3. Click "Send Request" above any request line below.
###   4. Requests are chained using variables: running them top-to-bottom
###      populates IDs automatically.
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@contentType = application/json
@sessionId = dev-user-default
@altSessionId = user-secondary

### ====================================================================
### 1. HEALTH CHECK
### ====================================================================

### 1.1 Service Health Check
# Checks backend uptime and service readiness
# @name healthCheck
GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json


### ====================================================================
### 2. JOURNAL ENTRIES LIFECYCLE (CRUD & OPTIMISTIC CONCURRENCY)
### ====================================================================

### 2.1 Create a New Journal Entry
# Persists a new journal entry with initial revision = 1
# @name createEntry
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "title": "Mi primer día en Madrid",
  "targetLanguage": "es",
  "explanationLanguage": "en",
  "content": "Hoy fue un día increíble. Caminé por el Parque del Retiro y visité el Museo del Prado."
}

### Capture created entry ID
@createdEntryId = {{createEntry.response.body.id}}

### 2.2 List All Journal Entries for Current User
# Returns entries in reverse chronological order
# @name listEntries
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

### 2.3 Get Specific Journal Entry by ID
# Retrieves single entry ensuring ownership
# @name getEntryById
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries/{{createdEntryId}} HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

### 2.4 Update Existing Journal Entry (Revision Concurrency Check)
# Updates content with expectedRevision = 1; revision increments to 2
# @name updateEntrySuccess
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "id": "{{createdEntryId}}",
  "title": "Mi primer día en Madrid (Actualizado)",
  "targetLanguage": "es",
  "explanationLanguage": "en",
  "content": "Hoy fue un día increíble. Caminé por el Parque del Retiro, visité el Museo del Prado y comí tapas.",
  "expectedRevision": 1
}

### 2.5 Conflict Check: Attempt Update with Stale Revision (Expects 409 Conflict)
# Verifies optimistic locking detects stale revision 1 when entry is at revision 2
# @name updateEntryConflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "id": "{{createdEntryId}}",
  "title": "Actualización obsoleta",
  "targetLanguage": "es",
  "explanationLanguage": "en",
  "content": "Este intento debe fallar con REVISION_CONFLICT.",
  "expectedRevision": 1
}


### ====================================================================
### 3. AI LINGUISTIC ANALYSIS (STAGE 1 CORE FLOW)
### ====================================================================

### 3.1 Submit Journal Entry Text for AI Feedback
# Runs linguistic analysis, saves analysis snapshot, and returns validated suggestions with UTF-16 offsets
# @name analyzeEntry
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries/analyze HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "title": "Práctica con errores",
  "targetLanguage": "es",
  "explanationLanguage": "en",
  "content": "Hola, yo comer mucho caliente esta manana."
}

### Capture returned IDs from analysis
@analyzedEntryId = {{analyzeEntry.response.body.entryId}}
@analysisId = {{analyzeEntry.response.body.id}}
@suggestionId0 = {{analyzeEntry.response.body.suggestions[0].id}}

### 3.2 Retrieve Analysis Details & Suggestions by Analysis ID
# Fetches immutable analysis snapshot and its suggestions
# @name getAnalysisById
GET {{baseUrl}}/analyses/{{analysisId}} HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}


### ====================================================================
### 4. MANUAL ANALYSIS SNAPSHOT INGESTION
### ====================================================================

### 4.1 Create Entry Specifically for Manual Analysis Ingestion
# @name createEntryForManualAnalysis
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "title": "Entrada para Análisis Manual",
  "targetLanguage": "es",
  "explanationLanguage": "en",
  "content": "Yo comer manzanas ayer."
}

@manualEntryId = {{createEntryForManualAnalysis.response.body.id}}

### 4.2 Ingest Analysis Snapshot with Strict Offsets & Rules
# Validates category, UTF-16 bounds, and records snapshot
# @name ingestAnalysisSnapshot
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyses HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "entryId": "{{manualEntryId}}",
  "entryRevision": 1,
  "sourceText": "Yo comer manzanas ayer.",
  "taxonomyVersion": "1.0.0",
  "modelVersion": "manual-v1",
  "promptVersion": "v1",
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "category": "grammar_syntax",
      "ruleCode": "grammar.verb_tense",
      "kind": "correction",
      "startOffset": 3,
      "endOffset": 8,
      "originalText": "comer",
      "replacementText": "comí",
      "explanationTitle": "Pretérito indefinido",
      "explanationMessage": "Usa 'comí' para acciones concluidas en el pasado."
    }
  ]
}

@ingestedSuggestionId = {{ingestAnalysisSnapshot.response.body.suggestions[0].id}}


### ====================================================================
### 5. DECISIONS ENGINE (ACCEPT / DISMISS SUGGESTIONS)
### ====================================================================

### 5.1 Accept Suggestion & Apply Edit to Entry
# Reconstructs text right-to-left and advances entry revision
# @name acceptDecision
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries/{{manualEntryId}}/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "expectedRevision": 1,
  "requestId": "req-decision-accept-001",
  "decisions": [
    {
      "suggestionId": "{{ingestedSuggestionId}}",
      "action": "accepted"
    }
  ]
}

### 5.2 Idempotency Test: Resend Identical Decision Request
# Verifies that sending the exact same requestId returns the cached result without duplicate side-effects
# @name idempotentDecisionRetry
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries/{{manualEntryId}}/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "expectedRevision": 1,
  "requestId": "req-decision-accept-001",
  "decisions": [
    {
      "suggestionId": "{{ingestedSuggestionId}}",
      "action": "accepted"
    }
  ]
}

### 5.3 Dismiss Suggestion (from AI Analysis entry)
# Records dismissed decision without modifying entry text
# @name dismissDecision
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries/{{analyzedEntryId}}/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "expectedRevision": 1,
  "requestId": "req-decision-dismiss-002",
  "decisions": [
    {
      "suggestionId": "{{suggestionId0}}",
      "action": "dismissed"
    }
  ]
}


### ====================================================================
### 6. LEARNING INSIGHTS & ANALYTICS (STAGE 2 EXTENSION)
### ====================================================================

### 6.1 Get User Learning Insights & Trends
# Computes totals, decision distribution, categorical breakdown, top mistakes, and chronological trends
# @name getInsights
GET {{baseUrl}}/insights HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}


### ====================================================================
### 7. MULTI-TENANCY, AUTHENTICATION & ERROR HANDLING
### ====================================================================

### 7.1 Verify Multi-Tenant Isolation (Alt User List)
# Secondary user with alt session ID should not see primary user's private entries
# @name altUserListEntries
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{altSessionId}}

### 7.2 Access Denied / Ownership Enforcement (Expects 403 Forbidden)
# Secondary user attempts to read primary user's private entry
# @name forbiddenCrossTenantAccess
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries/{{createdEntryId}} HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{altSessionId}}

### 7.3 Non-Existent Resource (Expects 404 Not Found)
# @name entryNotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 HTTP/1.1
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

### 7.4 Request Validation Error (Expects 422 Unprocessable Entity)
# Missing required targetLanguage field
# @name validationErrorMissingField
POST {{baseUrl}}/entries HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
X-Session-ID: {{sessionId}}

{
  "title": "Entrada Inválida",
  "content": "Falta el campo targetLanguage requerido."
}
